Generic single-database configuration.

Schema management
-----------------

The app still calls `Base.metadata.create_all()` on boot (see
`app.main._ensure_db_tables`), which creates missing tables but never alters an
existing one. Alembic is what tracks the alterations.

Fresh database:

    DATABASE_URL=... alembic upgrade head

Existing database (tables already created by create_all) — adopt the baseline
without re-running it, otherwise the first CREATE TABLE fails:

    DATABASE_URL=... alembic stamp 754e61405945

After changing a model:

    DATABASE_URL=... alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
    # review the generated file, then
    DATABASE_URL=... alembic upgrade head

`alembic/env.py` imports every model module explicitly. A model that is not
imported there is invisible to --autogenerate and will be silently dropped from
the diff, so add new model modules to that list.

The hand-rolled ALTERs in `app.database.ensure_user_usage_columns` predate this
setup. They are idempotent and fail loudly on anything other than "column
already exists"; new columns should go through Alembic instead.
